    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "CAG acts as 'friend, philosopher, and guide' to the Public Accounts Committee (PAC).",
        "Finance Commission recommendations are strictly advisory and not legally binding on the central government.",
        "CAG is removed in the same manner and grounds as a Supreme Court Judge, whereas FC members are eligible for reappointment."
      ],
      "id": "ytbg5jz"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Comptroller and Auditor General (CAG) audits all expenditure from the Consolidated Fund of India and States under Article 148.",
        "The Finance Commission is constituted under Article 280 to allocate tax proceeds between the Union and the States.",
        "CAG serves as the guardian of the public purse and assists the Parliament's Public Accounts Committee.",
        "Finance Commission recommendations are advisory in nature and laid before Parliament by the President."
      ],
      "id": "p6hamd1"
    }
